{"text": " So what's the next step on the latter? 2100, that morning hasn't happened yet, but we can follow the evidence. Every video you watch, every question you ask an AI runs in a data center. In 2024, data centers used about one and a half percent of the world's electricity. The international energy agency expects that to more than double by 2030. That's slightly more than all of Japan uses today. Meanwhile, in 2023, a small Caltech satellite called Maple transmitted power wirelessly in space and aimed to signal at a rooftop in Pasadena. Tiny, but it worked. So here's one scenario, not a fact. The internet, AI, and whole cities running more and more on sunlight. Some of it may be collected in orbit where the sun never sets. In 1500, the sun decided when you went to sleep. In 2100, it might decide whether your AI wakes up. The sun won't notice. NASA estimates it has another 5 billion years or so. The question is, what will have learned to do with it?", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.62, "text": " So what's the next step on the latter?", "tokens": [50364, 407, 437, 311, 264, 958, 1823, 322, 264, 18481, 30, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13555786257884542, "compression_ratio": 1.5513698630136987, "no_speech_prob": 0.009490210562944412, "words": [{"word": " So", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.9488697052001953}, {"word": " what's", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9437626302242279}, {"word": " the", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.58, "probability": 0.9983899593353271}, {"word": " next", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.82, "probability": 0.9988823533058167}, {"word": " step", "start": 0.82, "end": 1.02, "probability": 0.998877227306366}, {"word": " on", "start": 1.02, "end": 1.2, "probability": 0.9956682920455933}, {"word": " the", "start": 1.2, "end": 1.32, "probability": 0.9979367256164551}, {"word": " latter?", "start": 1.32, "end": 1.62, "probability": 0.5346215963363647}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.48, "e